1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,740
Most people can see at least a million different colours, but have you ever thought why they're important?
大多数人至少能看见一百万种不同的颜色，但你是否想过它们为什么重要？

2
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:11,530
Colours often have meanings and act as signs.
颜色常常代表某种意义并充当标志。

3
00:00:11,530 --> 00:00:15,840
They're a way of communicating, even when we don't notice them.
它们是一种交流方式，即使在我们没有注意到它们的时候也是如此。

4
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:21,000
The development of colours in the environment may be linked to the science of evolution.
环境中颜色的发展可能与进化科学有关。

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,110
As living organisms developed a sense of vision, they were able to explore the environment around them.
随着生物体发展出视觉，它们能够探索周围的环境。

6
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:37,490
As vision developed and living creatures became able to distinguish colours, fruits began to use them to attract animals to propagate their seeds.
随着视觉的发展，生物能够区分颜色，果实开始利用颜色吸引动物来传播种子。

7
00:00:37,490 --> 00:00:46,140
Flowers developed bright colours to attract pollinators, and venomous or poisonous animals were able to use their bold shades as a warning.
花朵发展出鲜艳的颜色来吸引传粉者，而有毒（通过蛰、咬）或有毒（通过吃、接触、吸入）的动物能够利用它们醒目的颜色作为警告。

8
00:00:46,140 --> 00:00:51,240
Humans have also evolved to use these signs to interpret the world.
人类也进化出利用这些标志来解读世界的能力。

9
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:59,650
Colour is often an indication that tells us when fruit or vegetables can be eaten, that they're not unripe or rotten.
颜色常常是一种指示，告诉我们水果或蔬菜何时可以食用，表明它们不是未成熟或腐烂的。

10
00:00:59,650 --> 00:01:04,030
We've also developed our own colour signals to communicate.
我们还发展出了自己的颜色信号来进行交流。

11
00:01:04,030 --> 00:01:11,380
The red of a traffic light or a warning sign tells us about potential dangers or the precautions we need to take.
交通灯或警示牌的红色告诉我们潜在的危险或需要采取的预防措施。

12
00:01:11,380 --> 00:01:16,870
Electrical wires use different colours to tell us how to connect them safely.
电线使用不同的颜色来告诉我们如何安全地连接它们。

13
00:01:16,870 --> 00:01:20,580
Colours can be used as signifiers in more complex ways.
颜色可以以更复杂的方式作为信号象征。

14
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:33,390
Meanings can be transferred into different contexts – food products are sometimes labelled with red, yellow or green according to their nutritional content, borrowing the colours from traffic signals.
意义可以被转移到不同的情境中——食品有时会借用交通信号灯的颜色，根据其营养成分被贴上红色、黄色或绿色的标签。

15
00:01:33,390 --> 00:01:35,780
Some signs are less obvious.
有些标志则不那么明显。

16
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:44,660
Consumer brands use different colours in their logos, packaging, products, and advertising to send us messages about their values.
消费品牌在其商标、包装、产品和广告中使用不同的颜色来向我们传达关于其价值观的信息。

17
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:55,330
For example, luxury goods often use dark but intense colours as a mark of quality, while those aimed at children use bold, bright colours.
例如，奢侈品通常使用深色但强烈的颜色作为品质的标志，而面向儿童的产品则使用醒目、明亮的颜色。

18
00:01:55,330 --> 00:02:00,240
We might only notice this if companies use the 'wrong' colours.
只有当公司使用了"错误"的颜色时，我们才可能注意到这一点。

19
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:08,040
Studies have shown that people are less likely to buy something if it's branded with an inappropriate colour.
研究表明，如果某种产品的品牌颜色不合适，人们购买它的可能性就会降低。

20
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:17,620
Whether human-made or natural, and whether we consciously notice them or not, colours tell us a lot about the world around us.
无论是人造的还是自然的，无论我们是否有意识地注意到它们，颜色都告诉我们很多关于我们周围世界的信息。
